/** @page playback_system Playback System
 *  @brief Overview of MIDI playback components in Maestro MPTK.
 *
 *  @details
 *  This section introduces the components and workflows involved in MIDI playback.
 *  The two main user-facing playback components are:
 *  - MidiFilePlayer for complete MIDI file playback,
 *  - MidiStreamPlayer for real-time event-driven playback.
 *
 *  Playback-related features typically include:
 *  - selecting MIDI files,
 *  - loading MIDI content,
 *  - controlling playback,
 *  - inspecting timing and position,
 *  - reacting to playback events,
 *  - sending real-time MIDI events and stopping notes,
 *  - building chords and scale-based harmony (Maestro Pro),
 *  - using extended Maestro Pro playback features.
 *
 *  @section playback_start Quick Start
 *
 *  @code
 *  MidiFilePlayer player = FindObjectOfType<MidiFilePlayer>();
 *  player.MPTK_MidiName = "Bach_Prelude";
 *  player.MPTK_Play();
 *  @endcode
 *
 *  @section playback_pages Related Pages
 *
 *  Read these pages in the following order:
 *
 *  - @subpage midifileplayer_overview
 *  - @subpage midifileplayer_loading
 *  - @subpage midifileplayer_playback
 *  - @subpage midifileplayer_position
 *  - @subpage midifileplayer_events
 *  - @subpage midifileplayer_pro
 *  - @subpage midistreamplayer_overview
 *  - @subpage midistreamplayer_realtime
 *  - @subpage midistreamplayer_chords
 *  - @subpage midistreamplayer_pro
 *  - @subpage mptkevent_concept
 *  - @subpage mptkchannels_concept
 *  - @subpage mptkwriter_concept
 *  - @subpage maestro_pro_features
 *
 *  @section playback_modules Related Modules
 *
 *  - @ref playback_and_sequencing
 *  - @ref midifileplayer_management
 *  - @ref midistreamplayer_management
 *  - @ref midi_data_model
 *  - @ref runtime_services
 *  - @ref pro_playback_prefabs
 *  - @ref diagnostics_tools
 *  - @ref synth_engine
 *
 *  @section playback_next Next Steps
 *
 *  - @ref getting_started
 *  - @ref detailed_guides
 *  - @ref workflows
 */
